#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Grain for the North"
msgstr "Kuzeye Tahıl"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hunters send news: the summer in the north was cold, and their families have no grain. My ship "
"leaves in three days: fill it with twelve crates!"
msgstr ""
"Avcılarımdan haber var: kuzeyde yaz soğuk geçmiş, ailelerinin hiç tahılı yok. Gemim üç gün sonra "
"kalkıyor: onu on iki sandıkla {crew|doldur|doldur|doldurun}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve crates! Nobody in the north goes hungry this winter. The whole valley thanks you."
msgstr ""
"On iki sandık! Bu kış kuzeyde kimse aç kalmayacak. Bütün vadi {crew|sana|sana|size} teşekkür "
"ediyor."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the harvest failed, the farms helped each other: next year, it might be them."
msgstr "Hasat kötü geçince çiftlikler birbirine yardım ederdi: gelecek yıl sıra onlara gelebilirdi."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wool Fair"
msgstr "Yün Panayırı"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The wool fair! Traders come from the Long Lake to buy. Bring me eight crates of wool, the more the"
" better, and the fair is a success."
msgstr ""
"Yün panayırı! Uzun Göl'den tüccarlar almaya geliyor. Bana sekiz sandık yün "
"{crew|getir|getir|getirin}, ne kadar çok o kadar iyi; panayır da başarılı olsun."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eight crates! The traders from the Long Lake ask: who are these girls? I say: the best traders of "
"the Home Lakes."
msgstr ""
"Sekiz sandık! Uzun Göl'ün tüccarları soruyor: {crew|bu çocuk kim|bu kız kim|bu çocuklar kim|bu "
"kızlar kim}? Ben de diyorum ki: Yurt Gölleri'nin en iyi {crew|tüccarı|tüccarı|tüccarları}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool was so important that some sagas tell of whole ships full of it."
msgstr "Yün o kadar önemliydi ki bazı destanlar yün dolu gemilerden söz eder."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Goats on the Island"
msgstr "Adadaki Keçiler"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My four goats swam to Bergö! They eat Dagny's flowers, and she is cross. Bring them back before "
"they eat her kiln too!"
msgstr ""
"Dört keçim yüzüp Bergö'ye gitmiş! Dagny'nin çiçeklerini yiyorlar, o da çok kızgın. Fırınını da "
"yemeden onları geri {crew|getir|getir|getirin}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My naughty goats! Tomorrow I build a higher fence. Here, my best cheese."
msgstr "Yaramaz keçilerim! Yarın daha yüksek bir çit yapacağım. {crew|Al|Al|Alın}, en iyi peynirim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, take them! They ate my flowers and a basket and a shoe!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Al|Al|Alın} onları, {crew|al|al|alın}! Çiçeklerimi, bir sepeti, bir de ayakkabıyı yediler!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats are good swimmers when they must be, and they eat nearly anything."
msgstr "Keçiler gerekince iyi yüzer ve neredeyse her şeyi yer."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "News for Everybody"
msgstr "Herkese Haber"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Büyük haber: Uzun Göl'den bir gemi gelecek, göller arasındaki yol açılıyor! Demirciye, Stormvik "
"balıkçılarına ve Hallvik'teki Orm'a {crew|söyle|söyle|söyleyin}. Gerisine ben söylerim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "Uzun Göl'den bir gemi mi? Demirimi isteyeceklerdir!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr "Yeni göller, yeni balıklar! Haber {crew|verdiğin|verdiğin|verdiğiniz} için teşekkürler."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Uzaklardan misafirler! Daha çok bira yapmalıyım. Teşekkürler, {crew|oğlum|kızım|çocuklar|kızlar}!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr ""
"Kuzeyin gölleri ırmaklarla ve teknelerin karadan sürüklendiği geçitlerle birbirine bağlıydı."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "Grim'e Bir İnek"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Yaşlandım, her sabah taze süt içmek isterim. Bana at çiftliğinden bir inek "
"{crew|getir|getir|getirin}. Kuğular kıskanacak!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"Bir inek! Adını Kuğu koyuyorum, ha. {crew|Al, zahmetin için, bir de yaşlı bir adamı yıllardır "
"ziyaret ettiğin için|Al, zahmetin için, bir de yaşlı bir adamı yıllardır ziyaret ettiğin "
"için|Alın, zahmetiniz için, bir de yaşlı bir adamı yıllardır ziyaret ettiğiniz için}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "İyi bir inek on yıl ya da daha uzun süre süt verir, ailenin bir parçası olurdu."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Tepede Çiçekler"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"Güneşli tepeye çiçek {crew|ek|ek|ekin}! Açınca Gudrun'un hanına üç sandık "
"{crew|götür|götür|götürün}: han yaz gibi koksun istiyor."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Çiçek tohumları toprakta. İki gün sonra açarlar."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"Her masada çiçek! Misafirler gülümsüyor. İşte {crew|gümüşün, bir de sana bir bardak süt|gümüşün, "
"bir de sana bir bardak süt|gümüşünüz, bir de her birinize bir bardak süt}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "Vikingler şölenler ve düğünler için çiçeklerden çelenk ve taç örerdi."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
